{{- /*
  visual_evidence_implement: tag-gated by the caller (frontend features
  only). Tells the implementer where to deposit rendered-state captures
  for any UI screen this iteration touches.

  The methodology — which harness to use, naming, storage, why it
  matters — lives in skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md and is loaded as
  a mandatory read for frontend-tagged features. This block stays
  thin: it just publishes the directory the harness expects so the
  reviewer's gate has something to look at.

  Returns "" when IterDir is empty.
*/ -}}
{{- define "visual_evidence_implement" -}}
{{ if .IterDir }}## Visual Evidence (when UI code changes this iteration)

If this iteration adds or modifies user-facing UI, capture the rendered state of each affected screen into:

    {{ .IterDir }}/screenshots/

See skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md (loaded as a mandatory read for this feature) for the full methodology: which harness to use, naming, storage, why it matters. The reviewer on the next hop reads any files it finds in that directory and cannot approve UI changes without them.

If this iteration touches no UI code, the directory's absence is expected.

{{ end }}{{- end -}}
